## A Grim Milestone: Food Recalls Hit 759 for 2026

The food recall landscape seems to be on a trajectory of disappointment this year, with a startling 759 recalls reported so far. This places 2026 on track to surpass recall records, potentially exceeding 2025's peak months.

## July's Top Offenders

July 1st alone saw an alarming number of recalls:

- **Spring & Mulberry Inc.** has landed itself in hot water again, recalling multiple chocolate products due to potential Salmonella contamination. Already rated as one of the worst offenders in the industry, this brand further cements its position on the recall wall of shame.

- **Utz Quality Foods, LLC** made headlines with its recall of several potato chip varieties, citing potential Salmonella contamination--a classic case of a snack gone wrong.

- **Joy Gourmet Foods LLC.** withdrew batches of its lassi beverages for not meeting pasteurization standards, a concerning lapse in safety protocols.

- **Champion Foods, LLC** recalled its Motor City Pizza Co. Cheese Bread over potential Salmonella contamination, adding to consumers' wariness about processed foods.

## Repeat Offenders: Breaking Down the List

The food industry continues to grapple with brands notorious for repeated recalls. Spring & Mulberry Inc. leads with 11 recalls this year alone, all of which fall under the severe Class I category. Ghirardelli Chocolate Company and Moonlight Packing Corporation follow closely, with similarly grim records.

## Who Can We Trust?

When one sees the names of household brands frequently appearing on recall lists, it's natural to feel skeptical about product safety. The food safety measures in place seem insufficient to prevent these occurrences. While challenges in extensive supply chains are understandable, consumers deserve better--not just apologies and refunds but proactive solutions.

## The Salmonella Scourge

Reflecting on this month's recalls, Salmonella appears as a recurring antagonist. Of the many reasons for recalls, contamination with this pathogen remains a consistent and alarming issue. With 196 recalls attributed to Salmonella this year alone, it's high time the industry seriously reevaluates its standards.

## Final Thoughts

As consumers, remaining vigilant about the brands we purchase from is a necessary safeguard--one frustratingly forced upon us due to industry failings. However, accountability from corporations must be prioritized to address these persistent food safety issues. Until then, check your shelves, read labels, and stay informed.

## The Brands under Recall

The following brands have been implicated in recent food recalls:

- Spring & Mulberry Inc.
- Utz Quality Foods, LLC
- Joy Gourmet Foods LLC.
- Champion Foods, LLC

To stay safe, consider avoiding the recalled products from these brands.
